// Template for Config/Secrets.xcconfig, which is git-ignored.
//
// Copy this file to Secrets.xcconfig and fill in the value. The build reads it
// into Info.plist as MALClientID; `AppConfiguration` reads it back at runtime.
//
// Note on what this is and isn't: MAL's OAuth flow uses PKCE and has no client
// secret, so the client id is a public identifier rather than a credential — an
// attacker gains nothing from it. Keeping it out of the repo is still worth doing,
// because it means rotating it is a config change rather than a code change, and
// because nobody has to think about which committed strings are safe.
MAL_CLIENT_ID = your_client_id_here
